flowchart LR
  accTitle: Week 15 Integration Test Architecture
  accDescr: Flutter and API collection tests cross the HTTPS boundary into Laravel, which enforces validation and authorization before MySQL and simulated transport dependencies. Results are retained as evidence and defects feed the hardening backlog.
  flutter["Public client boundary&#58; Flutter Web states and validation"]
  collection["Test client boundary&#58; Postman and PowerShell collection"]
  https["HTTPS and CORS boundary"]
  middleware["Laravel API context&#58; session, role, correlation, headers"]
  controller["Workflow contract&#58; validation, pagination, idempotency"]
  database["MariaDB controlled fixture store"]
  transport["Simulated notification and secure exchange dependency"]
  failure["Controlled timeout, unavailable service, duplicate, rollback"]
  evidence["Sanitized results, logs, screenshots, JUnit"]
  backlog["Defect record, priority, fix, retest, remaining risk"]
  flutter -->|normal and UI adverse states| https
  collection -->|positive, negative, boundary, auth| https
  https -->|JSON plus bearer token| middleware
  middleware -->|authorized actor and correlation ID| controller
  controller -->|transactional state| database
  controller -->|bounded external work| transport
  failure -.->|safe loading and error feedback| flutter
  failure -.->|retry, rollback, manual review| controller
  flutter -->|widget and browser evidence| evidence
  collection -->|expected versus actual| evidence
  middleware -->|safe correlated outcomes| evidence
  evidence -->|evidence-supported finding| backlog
  backlog -->|targeted retest and regression| collection
%% portable-canonical-v2:--
